  "raw_text": "309\n\nVERBS WITH ROOTS THAT END WITH AN \"I\" /\n\nVERBOS\n \nCON RAÍCES QUE TERMINAN CON UNA \"I\"\n\n5 Verbs With Roots That End With An \"I\" / 5 Verbos Con Raíces Que Terminan Con Una \"I\"\n\n(Briaia\n,\n \nDiaia\n,\n \nPiaia\n,\n \nSwiaia, Wiaia)\n\nThe purple highlighted letter is extra in comparison to a regular verb conjugation. /\n\nLa letra\n \npúrpura\n \nresaltada es extra en comparación con una conjugación verbal regular.\n\nPresent\n \nI /\nPresente I\n\nPresent II /\nPresente II\n\nPast I /\nPasado I\n\nPast II /\nPasado II\n\nFuture I /\nFuturo I\n\nFuture II /\nFuturo II\n\nYang (1\nst\n/1\ner\n)\n \nBrisuna\n \nBrisna*\n \nBrisatna\n \nBriri\n \nBriaisna\n \nBrimna**\n\nMan (2\nnd\n/2\ndo\n)\n \nBrisuma\n \nBrisma*\n \nBrisatma\n \nBriram\n \nBriaisma\n \nBrima\n\nWitin(3\nrd\n/3\ner\n),Yawan\n \nBrisuya\n \nBrisa*\n \nBrisata\n \nBrin**\n \nBriaisa\n \nBribia\n\nPresent\n \nI /\nPresente I\n\nPresent II /\nPresente II\n\nPast I /\nPasado I\n\nPast II /\nPasado II\n\nFuture I /\nFuturo I\n\nFuture II /\nFuturo II\n\nYang (1\nst\n/1\ner\n)\n \nDisuna\n \nDisna*\n \nDisatna\n \nDiri\n \nDiaisna\n \nDimna**\n\nMan (2\nnd\n/2\ndo\n)\n \nDisuma\n \nDisma*\n \nDisatma\n \nDiram\n \nDiaisma\n \nDima\n\nWitin(3\nrd\n/3\ner\n),Yawan\n \nDisuya\n \nDisa*\n \nDisata\n \nDin**\n \nDiaisa\n \nDibia\n\nPresent\n \nI /\nPresente I\n\nPresent II /\nPresente II\n\nPast I /\nPasado I\n\nPast II /\nPasado II\n\nFuture I /\nFuturo I\n\nFuture II /\nFuturo II\n\nYang (1\nst\n/1\ner\n)\n \nPisuna\n \nPisna*\n \nPisatna\n \nPiri\n \nPiaisna\n \nPimna**\n\nMan (2\nnd\n/2\ndo\n)\n \nPisuma\n \nPisma*\n \nPisatma\n \nPiram\n \nPiaisma\n \nPima\n\nWitin(3\nrd\n/3\ner\n),Yawan\n \nPisuya\n \nPisa*\n \nPisata\n \nPin**\n \nPiaisa\n \nPibia\n\nPresent\n \nI /\nPresente I\n\nPresent II /\nPresente II\n\nPast I /\nPasado I\n\nPast II /\nPasado II\n\nFuture I /\nFuturo I\n\nFuture II /\nFuturo II\n\nYang (1\nst\n/1\ner\n)\n \nSwisuna\n \nSwisna*\n \nSwisatna\n \nSwiri\n \nSwiaisna\n \nSwimna**\n\nMan (2\nnd\n/2\ndo\n)\n \nSwisuma\n \nSwisma*\n \nSwisatma\n \nSwiram\n \nSwiaisma\n \nSwima\n\nWitin(3\nrd\n/3\ner\n),Yawan\n \nSwisuya\n \nSwisa*\n \nSwisata\n \nSwin**\n \nSwiaisa\n \nSwibia\n\nPresent\n \nI /\nPresente I\n\nPresent II /\nPresente II\n\nPast I /\nPasado I\n\nPast II /\nPasado II\n\nFuture I /\nFuturo I\n\nFuture II /\nFuturo II\n\nYang (1\nst\n/1\ner\n)\n \nWisuna\n \nWisna*\n \nWisatna\n \nWiri\n \nWiaisna\n \nWimna**\n\nMan (2\nnd\n/2\ndo\n)\n \nWisuma\n \nWisma*\n \nWisatma\n \nWiram\n \nWiaisma\n \nWima\n\nWitin(3\nrd\n/3\ner\n),Yawan\n \nWisuya\n \nWisa*\n \nWisata\n \nWin**\n \nWiaisa\n \nWibia\n\nImperative / Imperativa:\n \nBris\n,\n \nDis\n,\n \nPis\n,\n \nSwis\n,\n \nWis\n\nProhibitive / Prohibitiva:\n \nBri\npara\n,\n \nDi\npara\n,\n \nPi\npara\n,\n \nSwi\npara\n,\n \nWi\npara\n\nNegative / Negativa:\n \nBri\nras\n,\n \nDi\nras\n,\n \nPi\nras\n,\n \nSwi\nras\n,\n \nWi\nras\n\nPresent participle/ Participio presente:\n \nBri\n,\n \nDi\n,\n \nPi\n,\n \nSwi\n,\n \nWi\n\n*\n \nThe\n \nletter “\ni\n” is removed from the conjugation, leaving only the “\ni\n” from the root\n \n/\n\nLa letra \"\ni\n\" se elimina de la conjugación, dejando solo la \"\ni\n\" de la raíz\n\n**\n \nThe letter “\na\n” is removed from the conjugation\n \n/\n\nLa letra \"\na\n\" se elimina de la\n \nconjugación",
